\
Tears of the Kingdom has a fairly lengthy tutorial, and for good reason \'97 not only has it been six years since Breath of the Wild came out, but you've also got four brand-new abilities to mess about with.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nintendolife.com/guides/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom-great-sky-island-walkthrough-shrines-closed-door-quest-abilities"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 The Great Sky Island}}\'a0is where you start your adventure, and you get all four abilities \'97 Ultrahand, Fuse, Ascend, and Recall \'97 over the course of the adventure. think Great Plateau and you're not far off. The game teaches you how to use all of these, and gives you a general idea of the ways you can interact with the world through the Shrines and by simply exploring and talking to the Constructs.\
Put simply, there's no need to rush off the island to reach the surface straight away. Take your time, explore the island, and simply enjoy yourself.\
\
When you first get to Hyrule, you can basically go wherever you want. But we recommend progressing with the story for a minute, at least until you unlock the first Skyview Tower and you get your paraglider.\
That means completing the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nintendolife.com/guides/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom-to-the-kingdom-of-hyrule-quest-where-to-find-lookout-landing#zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom-to-the-kingdom-of-hyrule"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 To the Kingdom of Hyrule}}\'a0quest. You should also pick up the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nintendolife.com/guides/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom-how-to-get-autobuild#how-to-complete-camera-work-in-the-depths"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Camera Work in the Depths}}\'a0quest from Josha to get your camera upgrade for your Purah Pad.\
When you get the Regional Phenomena quest, you'll be directed towards four different objective markers. You can do these in any order, but we have a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nintendolife.com/guides/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom-regional-phenomena-order-which-region-should-i-visit-first"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 recommended story route}}\'a0for you.\
\
Weapon durability returns, but in Tears of the Kingdom, it feels like weapons are\'a0
\f1\i \cb2 \strokec3 everywhere
\f0\i0 \cb2 \strokec3 . Enemies drop them, swords are often just lying around, and in caves, you'll often find swords buried underneath rocks.\
Basically, don't be afraid to fight things and don't be afraid to break things. You'll get replacements all the time. Check out our guide for the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nintendolife.com/guides/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom-best-weapons-where-to-find-best-fuses-early-weapons#best-early-game-weapons"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2\b \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Best Early-Game Weapons}}\'a0for more info.\
\
