Zonaite is a pretty rare material (at least until you explore the Depths), but it's also an extremely valuable one that you can use to buy items to upgrade your\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nintendolife.com/guides/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom-how-to-increase-battery-upgrade-energy-cells"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \cb2 \strokec4 Energy Cells}}, the battery power used to power Zonai Devices.\
Zonaite can be spent at the Forge Construct on the Great Sky Island to buy Crystallized Charges. These charges can be used at the\'a0
\f2\b \cb2 \strokec3 Crystal Refinery
\f0\b0 \cb2 \strokec3 , which you can access by warping to\'a0
\f2\b \cb2 \strokec3 Nachoyah Shrine
\f0\b0 \cb2 \strokec3 . Don't sell them for Rupees because Energy Cells are much more important later on in the game.\
\
While you can eventually build some pretty elaborate creations in Tears of the Kingdom, nothing is better than a good ol' horse to get you started.\
As early as Central Hyrule, you can find horses grazing about in the fields. Capturing these is the exact same as in Breath of the Wild \'97 sneak up on them and press 'A' when you're close enough to right. Give them a pat with the 'L' button, and then you're off. Horses make for a safe way of getting around too, as they naturally follow the roads of Hyrule.\
